This is a fork of fx (https://github.com/vercel-labs/fx), licensed Apache-2.0.

Modifications by Unbound Security, all confined to the browser (wasm) host:
- src/core/hosts/runtime_profile.zig: enable the `skills` capability for the
  wasm host profile.
- src/main.zig: give the wasm skill root policy native's workspace roots, use
  that policy for interactive refreshes, and poll the refresh on every host.
- src/core/skills/skill_runtime.zig: skip realpath canonicalisation on wasi,
  which has no realpath(3).
- src/builtins/browser_workspace_tools.zig, src/core/tooling/tool_runtime.zig:
  advertise and dispatch fx's own `skill` tool next to the browser shell.
- src/core/hosts/js_host_term_tools.zig (new), src/main.zig,
  src/core/app/app_agent_runtime.zig: let the browser terminal take host tools
  the way createFxAgent does, advertised as dynamic tools and run through
  js_host_tools. The page uses this to hand fx an MCP client's tools.
- src/core/hosts/js_host_term_tools.zig, src/main.zig,
  src/core/app/app_commands.zig, src/core/app/app_agent_runtime.zig: on the
  browser terminal, hand `/mcp` to the host, which runs MCP servers in the page,
  and load the host's tools again before a prompt when the host changed them.
- sdk/memfs.js (new): a read-only in-memory WASI filesystem.
- sdk/fx-sdk.js: back the WASI read calls with that filesystem when the host
  supplies `files`, instead of returning ENOTCAPABLE; accept `tools` in
  createFxTerminal, as createFxAgent already does, and let the host replace
  them (setTools) and answer `/mcp` (mcpCommand).

Purpose: make fx skills load and run in a browser host exactly as they do in
native fx, and let a browser terminal use host tools (for MCP) as the browser
agent already can, with servers added through fx's own `/mcp` command.
